repository-code: "https://github.com/Leonardini/TournamentsBeyond5Voters"
abstract: >-
  Code, tournaments, verdicts and machine-checked certificates for the
  paper "Tournaments not inducible by five voters", which proves
  13 <= N(5) <= 23, where N(k) is the least order at which some
  tournament is not the majority tournament of any k linear orders. The
  upper bound comes from proving that the Paley tournament on 23
  vertices is not 5-inducible; the lower bound from an exhaustive case
  analysis at order 12. Includes the depth-first placement search engine,
  the dissent-Boolean SAT encoding and cube tooling, independent witness
  verifiers that share no code with the search, and the per-cube sha256
  chains from which both published certificate roots rebuild.
keywords:
  - tournaments
  - majority voting
  - k-majority digraphs
  - Paley tournament
  - cube and conquer
  - SAT
  - LRAT
  - reproducibility
